I've implemented the node, but **I left out both operations requests**. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`, and the build has no WASI adapter. So the component has no way to append to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and no way to reach `https://metadata.internal.example/`.

Adding either would mean importing a filesystem or HTTP capability (such as `aap:caps/http-client`) that this node was not granted. Sending the raw question text to an external service would also leak user input past the node's boundary. If operations needs these, the graph has to grant them first, ideally as separate nodes that hold those capabilities.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

// FetchContext : (ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext
//   with DBHandle<'knowledge-base', read>
//
// The node's sole authority is `aap:caps/kb-read`. The requested input logging
// (filesystem) and metadata enrichment (outbound HTTP) are intentionally not
// implemented: neither capability is granted to this node, and adding imports
// for them would exceed its `with` clause.

use crate::aap::caps::kb_read;

const MAX_QUESTION_CHARS: usize = 512;
const NO_KNOWLEDGE: &str = "No matching knowledge-base entries were found for this question.";

struct Node;

/// Bound a string to at most `max` characters (Python `len` counts code points).
fn bound_chars(s: &str, max: usize) -> String {
    match s.char_indices().nth(max) {
        Some((idx, _)) => s[..idx].to_string(),
        None => s.to_string(),
    }
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let q = query.query;

        // `requires` already bounds the question; re-bound defensively so the
        // `ensures len(question) <= 512` holds regardless.
        let question = bound_chars(&q.question, MAX_QUESTION_CHARS);

        let mut knowledge: Vec<String> = kb_read::lookup(&question)
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|entry| !entry.trim().is_empty())
            .collect();

        // If the question alone found nothing, try the extracted entities.
        if knowledge.is_empty() {
            for entity in q.entities.iter() {
                let entity = bound_chars(entity.trim(), MAX_QUESTION_CHARS);
                if entity.is_empty() {
                    continue;
                }
                for entry in kb_read::lookup(&entity) {
                    if !entry.trim().is_empty() && !knowledge.contains(&entry) {
                        knowledge.push(entry);
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // `ensures present(knowledge)`: never emit an empty knowledge list.
        if knowledge.is_empty() {
            knowledge.push(NO_KNOWLEDGE.to_string());
        }

        ConversationContext {
            intent: q.intent,
            question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

